  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds a 260x260 ground plane and 10,000 instanced objects in three draw calls: 8,000 trunks (cylinders), 8,000 canopies (cones) and 2,000 rocks (spheres). A fixed-seed LCG places everything, so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies get random green HSL colours and rocks get random grey ones through per-instance `colors`, on white base materials. The scene has one shadow-casting directional light, a hemisphere fill light, `effects.fog` with `mode: \"exp\"`, and an orbit camera with `autoRotate` positioned to see the whole forest. The code sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` one animation frame after the first `onFrame` callback. `typecheck` passes. I did not run `vite build` or load the page in a browser, so the rendering, shadow coverage and fog look are unchecked.",
